ch session is 90 minutes. Resources available include a projector, whiteboards, and the 'Pasos 1' coursebook. For each session, list specific objectives, a timed breakdown of communicative activities, required materials, and a quick formative assessment method. Prioritize practical conversational skills, specifically ordering food, asking for directions, and shopping. Ensure a logical progression suited for adult learners with minimal out-of-class study time. Deliver a comprehensive unit plan only; no individual worksheets required.\n\nREADS: (none)\nWRITES: :result\nMCP-TOOLS: (none)\nBROWSER-TOOLS: (none)\n\n### Behavioral competencies (top 2 from corpus retrieval)\n1. Behavioral: Design (confidence: 0.95)\n   Why this fits: The task requires developing a structured, committable plan (a lesson sequence) from specific inputs (A1 objectives, session time, available resources) and constraints (adult learners, minimal study time). The 'Design' behavior's recommended pattern of structuring output into named sections with explicit decisions (breakdown of activities) and mapping against constraints perfectly fits the creation of a comprehensive unit plan.\n\n   Guidance (seed `:summary`):\n   Design produces a single committable plan/spec/architecture from inputs (goal + constraints + optional candidate options). Always structure as :map with named sections (decisions / open-questions / risks) — downstream automated stages bind on these. For non-trivial designs with interacting decisions, iterate via draft → critique → refined-spec. ALWAYS require an :open-questions field — empty means 'I'm confident', non-empty surfaces the gap before downstream stages run against an implicit guess. Composes into iterative-refinement (draft → critique → finalize) and sequential-pipeline (analysis → design → code-building) shells. Avoid when the task is option generation (use ideation) or execution against a known plan (use code-building).\n\nCapabilities:\n  - given a goal + constraints